{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Habiro.FlowSolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Habiro.FlowSolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.all_hold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.all_hold","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/FlowSolution.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The three propositions hold in the Habiro completion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.liTwoQ_volumetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.liTwoQ_volumetric","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/FlowSolution.lean#L60-L60","doc":"$\\mathrm{Li}_2^q$ is the formal Habiro antiderivative of\n$\\log_q(1+t)/t$, giving the volumetric expansion of the\nReeb-heat flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.fourier_diagonalises_qheat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.fourier_diagonalises_qheat","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/FlowSolution.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Categorical Fourier diagonalises $\\Delta_q$ on the\nPeter–Weyl decomposition of $\\mathbf{Rep}(\\mathrm{SU}_q(2))$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.expQ_solves_base_reeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.expQ_solves_base_reeb","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/FlowSolution.lean#L53-L53","doc":"$\\exp_q$ is the unique Habiro-grouplike satisfying\n$D_q \\exp_q = \\exp_q$.  Encoded as a proposition the\nconsumer must supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/FlowSolution.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.HabiroFlowSolution","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/FlowSolution.lean#L36-L63","doc":"The synthesis-level Habiro flow-solution class.  Conjectural:\nthe individual fixed-point properties are supplied by the\nexisting `QOU.QExponential`, `QOU.QDilogarithm`, and\n`QOU.CategoricalFourier` developments (structures, not\ntypeclasses — `HabiroFlowSolution` does NOT extend them).\nThis class records that the three hold *simultaneously* in a\ncommon Habiro completion and that their archimedean shadows\nunder $\\tau_\\infty$ are mutually compatible (the $\\tau_\\infty$\nof $\\mathrm{Li}_2^q$ gives the Bloch–Wigner volume function\nused by `prop:thurston-volume-additivity`, while\n$\\tau_\\infty(\\exp_q)$ gives the analytic exponential and\n$\\tau_\\infty(\\mathcal{F}_q)$ gives the classical Fourier\ntransform on the limit cocompact lattice). ","signatureChunk":0}]}